# ProfileFlow

> Lede 0.7.0's docs for ProfileFlow, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/profile.md

A hero flow for a profile: who this is, then the details, edited on the same page. A save is announced, and a failed save keeps the edits with an inline error.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/profile @lede/page
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md), [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md), [`avatar`](avatar.md), [`button`](button.md), [`form-section`](form-section.md), [`list`](list.md), [`page-header`](page-header.md) and [`text-field`](text-field.md), and the npm packages `@react-aria/live-announcer@^3.5.1`. It adds [`page`](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/page.md) only because the example below imports it. The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.7.0/profile.json.

## Import

```tsx
import { ProfileFlow } from '@/components/lede/flows/profile';
```

## Files and exports

| Installs to | Import from | Exports |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/lede/flows/profile.tsx` | `@/components/lede/flows/profile` | `ProfileFlow` (component), `Profile` (type), `ProfileFlowProps` (type) |

## Props

Hero flow: who this is, then the details, with editing one button away on the same page. A native `<form>` (Enter saves), with errors that say how to fix them and focus moved in and back out. A save is announced through a status region that is already in the page. A failed save keeps the form open with the person's edits.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `value` (required) | `Profile` |  |  |
| `onSave` (required) | `(next: Profile) => void \| Promise<void>` |  | Saves the edits. A returned promise keeps the form read-only until it settles. If it rejects, the edits stay and an inline error shows the rejection's message when it's an `Error` with one, or asks the person to try again. Throw an `Error` worded for the person: a fetch failure's own message, such as "Failed to fetch", shows as it is. |
| `back` | `{ href: string; label: string }` |  | Back link, such as `{ href: '/settings', label: 'Settings' }`. |

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { Page } from '@/components/lede/blocks/page';
import { ProfileFlow, type Profile } from '@/components/lede/flows/profile';

// A flow brings no gutter of its own: put it in Page, or in AppShell's main region.
export function ProfileScreen() {
  const [profile, setProfile] = useState<Profile>({ name: 'Ada Lovelace', email: 'ada@example.com' });
  return (
    <Page render={<main />} width="narrow">
      <ProfileFlow value={profile} onSave={setProfile} back={{ href: '/settings', label: 'Settings' }} />
    </Page>
  );
}
```

